          %blockquote
            %p or would follow, if that Example were argued properly
          %h3#in_simplicial_sets_2 In simplicial sets
          %h4#CofibrantReplacementAndHomotopyQuotientsFixedPoints Cofibrant replacement and homotopy quotients/fixed points
          %p
          #CofibrationsOfSimplicialActions.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (cofibrations of simplicial actions)
              %br/
              The cofibrations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSetCat
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSetCat\big(\mathbf{B}G_\bullet, sSet\big)_{proj}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BorelModelStructure"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the underlying morphism of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  is a relatively
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
                  on all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
                  not in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %p
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#DDK80"}> DDK 80, Prop. 2.2. (ii)
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou06"} Guillou 2006, Prop. 5.3
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine09"} Goerss &amp; Jardine 09, V Lem. 2.4 &amp; Cor. 2.10
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In particular this means that an object is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSetCat
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSetCat\big(\mathbf{B}G_\bullet, sSet\big)_{proj}
              if the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on it is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            %p
              Hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
              is obtained by forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} product
              with the model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G_\bullet
              for the total space of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet
              (see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              for notation and more details).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              It follows that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSetCat
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, A \in sSetCat\big(\mathbf{B}G_\bullet, sSet\big)_{proj}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R Hom_G(X,A)
            %p
              models the Borel
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
              (the underlying simplicial set is a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  if the
                  = succeed "-action" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is trivial, then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi G
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        R Hom_G(X,A)
                        \\simeq
                        Hom_G(W G \times X , A)
                        \\simeq
                        Hom(W G \times_G X, A)
                %p
                  is equivalently maps of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  out of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+construction"} Borel construction
                  on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \ast
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi h
                            %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        R Hom_G(X,A)
                        \\simeq
                        Hom_G(W G, A)
                        \\simeq
                        Hom(\overline{W} G , A)
                        \\simeq
                        A^{h G}
                %p
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+points"} homotopy fixed points
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
          %h4#RelationToSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace Relation to the slice over the simplicial classifying space
          %p
          #QuillenEquivalenceToSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            #eq:QuillenAdjunctionWithSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Qu
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ×
                          %mi W
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi W
                                %mo ¯
                              %mi G
                          %mi W
                          %mi G
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Qu
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Act\big(sSet_{Qu}\big)_{proj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{ \big((-) \times W G\big)/G }{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{ (-) \times_{\overline{W}G} W G  }{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\big(sSet_{Qu}\big)_{/\overline{W}G}
            %p
              which constitute a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction"} simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the Borel model structure (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BorelModelStructure"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+structure"} slice model structure
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+classifying+space"} simplicial classifying space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}G
            %p
          %p
            (this is essentially the statement of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DDK80"} DDK 80, Prop. 2.3, Prop. 2.4
          %p Here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+construction"} Borel construction
              %p
                understood as forming
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundles"} associated bundles
                to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundles"} universal principal bundles
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                forms
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
          %p
            (This may also be understood as an instance of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"}>
              fundamental theorem of
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            ”, see
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "slice+of+presheaves+is+presheaves+on+slice#InfinityActionsAsSlice"} there
          %p
          #SimplicialProofOfEquivalenceToSliceModelStructure.proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Consider any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mover
                            %mi W
                            %mo ¯
                          %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{/\overline{W}G}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi f
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi c
                                    %mi X
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi c
                                    %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi W
                              %mo ¯
                            %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp; \xrightarrow{\;\;f\;\;} &amp;&amp; Y
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {}_{\mathllap{c_X}}\searrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\swarrow_{\mathrlap{c_Y}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \overline{W}G
                    }
            %p
              Its image under the left adjoint functor is, by definition, the top left arrow in the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            %svg{:height => "127.679", :viewbox => "0 0 409.487 127.679", :width => "409.487", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
              %defs
                %g
                  %g{:id => "OU6JsEOflZ0H1y_2f39p0uDd6wQ=-glyph-0-0"}
                  %g{:id => "OU6JsEOflZ0H1y_2f39p0uDd6wQ=-glyph-0-1"}
