              %path{:d => "M -2.485276 2.867567 C -2.032151 1.148817 -1.020433 0.336317 -0.00090125 0.00038 C -1.020433 -0.335558 -2.032151 -1.148058 -2.485276 -2.870714 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "stroke-linecap" => "round", "stroke-linejoin" => "round", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "0.47818", :transform => "matrix(1, 0, 0, -1, 359.35637, 95.12538)"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "286.758", "xlink:href" => "#OU6JsEOflZ0H1y_2f39p0uDd6wQ=-glyph-2-7", :y => "102.931"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "291.343", "xlink:href" => "#OU6JsEOflZ0H1y_2f39p0uDd6wQ=-glyph-5-4", :y => "104.60475"}
            %p
              Here the right square and the total rectangle are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+squares"} Cartesian squares
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+squares"}> pullback squares
              ), by defnition of the functor. It follows by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              that also the square on the left is cartesian. Specifically, since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              are preserved under pullback, as shown, the top left morphism in question is the pullback of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              along a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %p
              It follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi G
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f) \underset{\overline{W}G}{\times} W G
              is:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a weak equivalence, because the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper model category
                  (see
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#Properness"} here
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a monomorphism, since monomorphisms are preserved by pullback (see
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "monomorphism#MonomorphismsArePreservedByPullback"} here
                %p
                  Moreover, since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi W
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \overline{W}G
                  is the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi c
                          %mi Y
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_Y^\ast(W G) \to Y
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+principal+bundle"} simplicial principal bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi c
                          %mi Y
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_Y^\ast(W G)
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
                %p
                  By Prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrationsOfSimplicialActions"}
                  this means that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munder
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mover
                              %mi W
                              %mo ¯
                            %mi G
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f) \underset{\overline{W}G}{\times} W G
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a cofibration.
            %p
              In summary, the left adjoint functor in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuillenAdjunctionWithSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace"} (4)
              preserves the classes of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              and of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
            %p Next…
          %p
            In fact, these functors
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuillenAdjunctionWithSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace"} (4)
            are
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            which induce an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
              equivalence of
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localizations"} simplicial localizations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %mi sSetCat
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %msub
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mi proj
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mover
                        %mi W
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W sSetCat\big(\mathbf{B}G_\bullet, sSet\big)_{proj} \simeq L_W sSet_{/\overline{W}H}
            (
            %a{:href => "#DDK80"}> DDK 80, Prop. 2.5
            ).
          %p
            This kind of relation is discussed in more detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
          %p
          #sSetEnrichmentOfAdjunctionToSliceOverSimpClassSpace.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (sSet-enrichement of the adjunction)
              %br/
              The statement that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuillenAdjunctionWithSliceOverSimplicialClassifyingSpace"} (4)
              is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+adjunction"} enriched adjunction
              is not made explicit in
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "#DDK80"} DDK 80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjunction
              (
              %a{:href => "#DDK80"}> DDK 80, Prop. 2.3
              ) and that they are each
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
              (
              %a{:href => "#DDK80"}> DDK 80, Prop. 2.4
              ).
            %p
              The remaining observation that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
            .maruku-equation
