              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofree+functor"} cofree
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi undrl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} undrl
              is familiar from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
              (see the section on
              %a{:href => "topological+G-space#CoinducedActions"} coinduced actions
              there), where it can be easily expressed point-wise in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CofreeSimplicialActionInComponents"} (6)
              adapts this idea to simplicial sets. Its form makes manifest that this gives a simplicial homomorphism, and with this the adjointness follows the usual logic by focusing on the image of the non-degenerate top-degree cell in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
