            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              holds. A sufficient condition that also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+axiom"} unit axiom
              hold is that all objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              are cofibrant.
          The following argument for the pushout-product axiom follows
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijk2006"} Berger &amp; Moerdijk (2006), Lem. 2.5.2
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It is sufficient to check the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              on (acyclic)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+cofibrations"} generating cofibrations
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "pushout-product#PushoutProductAxiomInCofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategories"} this remark
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+cofibrations"} generating cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;A \to B
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mi Act
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{\mathcal{G}Act(\mathbf{C})}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
                  is still a cofibration, which means that for any
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;Z \to W
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi WFib
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mi Act
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi undrl
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi WFib
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WFib_{\mathcal{G}Act(\mathbf{C})} = undrl^{-1} WFib_{\mathbf{C}}
            %p
              we need to find a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              in any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
