                    \\;\;\;\text{in}\;\; \mathbf{C}
                    \\,.
            %p But now using
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  that the underlying map of the previous
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
                  is still an acyclic fibration in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              %li
                %p
                  that the underlying maps of the previous
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  are still cofibrations in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RightQuillenInductionForBorelInCombSimpModCat"} (11)
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback-power+axiom"} pullback-power axiom
                  satisfied in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            %p
              it follows that the left map in this diagram is a cofibration and the right map is still an acyclic fibration, whence a lift exists by the model category axioms on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            %p
              A directly analogous argument applies in the cases where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              are in addition weak equivalences. Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              is verified.
            %p
              Finally, to verify the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+axiom"} unit axiom
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1} \,\in\, \mathbf{C}
              denotes the given
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}Act(\mathbf{C})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝟙
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathcal{G} \to \ast \overset{\mathbb{1}}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+action"} trivial action
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟙
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mi const
                        %mi 𝟙
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Q
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝟙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi const
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{const \mathbb{1}} \colon Q const(\mathbb{1}) \to const \mathbb{1}
              for a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{G}Act(\mathbf{C})
              the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mi const
                    %mi 𝟙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mrow
                            %mi const
                            %mi 𝕀
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mi 𝟙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi l
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Q const \mathbb{1})
                    \\otimes
                    X
                    \\overset{
                    p_{const \mathbb{I}} \otimes id_X
                    }{\longrightarrow}
                    (const \mathbb{1}) \otimes X
                    \\underoverset{\sim}{l}{\longrightarrow}
                    X
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            %p
              Since weak equivalence are just the underlying weak equivalences, for this it is sufficient (with the assumption that all objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              are cofibrant), that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory#KenBrownLemma"} Ken Brown’s lemma
            %p
              But the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is still cofibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RightQuillenInductionForBorelInCombSimpModCat"} (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes X
              is left Quillen by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              satisfied by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine+model+structure+on+topological+G-spaces"} fine model structure on topological G-spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel-equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} Borel-equivariant rational homotopy theory
          %h2#literature Literature
          %h3#ReferencesInSimplicialSets In simplicial sets
          %p
            The model structure, the characterization of its cofibrations, and its equivalence to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+structure"} slice model structure
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar W G
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#DDK80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emmanuel+Dror"}> Emmanuel Dror
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant maps which are self homotopy equivalences
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/2043448"} jstor:2043448
          %p This Quillen equivalence also mentioned as:
          %ul
            %li#Dwyer2008
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              , Exercise 4.2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory of classifying spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ku.dk/~jg/homotopical2008/Dwyer.CopenhagenNotes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dwyer_HomotopyTheoryOfClassifyingSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in relation to the “fine” model structure of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            which appears in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Guillou06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Guillou"}> Bert Guillou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A short note on models for equivariant homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~bertg/EquivModels.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GuillouModelsForEquivariantHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook account of (just) the Borel model structure:
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/19990208220238/http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/simp-sets/"} webpage
          %p
            Discussion with the model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groups"} simplicial groups
            replaced by groupal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+spaces"} Segal spaces
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prasma"}> Matan Prasma
              ,
              %em Segal Group Actions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.4749"}> arXiv:1311.4749
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            = succeed "-enhancement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
          %ul
            %li#BergerMoerdijk2006
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Boardman-Vogt resolution of operads in monoidal model categories
              %strong 45
              (2006) 807-849 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502155"}> arXiv:math/0502155
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.top.2006.05.001"} doi:10.1016/j.top.2006.05.001
          %p
            Discussion of a the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+model+structure"} integral model structure
            for actions of all simplicial groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prasma"} Matan Prasma
              %em The Grothendieck construction for model categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1404.1852"}> arXiv:1404.1852
              )
          %h3#ReferencesInTopologicalSpaces In topological spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Guillou06"} Guillou 2006, Section 5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steffen+Sagave"}> Steffen Sagave
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Schlichtkrull"} Christian Schlichtkrull
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Diagram spaces and symmetric spectra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.2764"} arXiv:1103.2764
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2012.07.013"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2012.07.013
        .revisedby
